  <revision rev="11" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ccbcf4152299741e39e915d215ea791c</srcmd5>
    <version>2.17.0</version>
    <time>1792076933</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- update to 2.17.0
  * Added bounded concurrent domain enumeration
  * Added crtname passive source
  * Added subdomaincenter passive source
  * Added Options -match-regex and -filter-regex to filter results with regular expressions
  * Fixed HIGH CVEs
  * Fixed response body leaks on error responses and unbounded GitHub rate-limit retries
  * Fixed dropped subdomains reported with uppercase letters or a trailing dot
  * Fixed ZoomEye source
  * Fixed data races between concurrent source runs
  * Fixed scanmalware statistics races between concurrent runs
  * Fixed HTTP connection reuse
  * feat(sources): honor -max-results across paginating sources
  * fix(extractor): match the target domain literally and reject partial hosts
  * fix(subscraping): cap untrusted source response bodies with a size limit
  * fix(subscraping): use DialContext instead of the deprecated Dial
  * feat: add scanmalware passive source
  * fix(crtsh): set statement_timeout via SQL query to avoid PgBouncer handshake rejection (#1828)
  * Added shodanct passive source
  * Added Option -vR, -virustotal-res for VirusTotal source
  * Added machine-readable source listing with -ls -oJ
  * Fixed source leaks
  * Fixed drain source channels on cancel so source goroutines exit instead of leaking on a blocked send
  * Fixed crtsh's query
  * Fixed VirusTotal source
  * Fixed Anubis source
  * Added the new Sub.md passive source, plus follow-up hardening for non-200 responses and context-aware error delivery
  * Fixed Netlas community-tier downloads
  * Fixed control-flow bugs across Hackertarget, IntelX, Shodan, C99, and Chinaz, including better transport error reporting and safer response validation
  * Fixed rate-limit handling so global and per-source limits work as expected, preserved per-source durations, and prevented nil map panics (forwarded request 1384987 from dheidler)</comment>
    <requestid>1385019</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
